-- 0029: lift the takhrij / grading clause into `hadith_entries.grading`.
--
-- In بلوغ المرام the grading is already in the matn — ibn Hajr closes each
-- hadith with who narrated it and how it was judged ("أخرجه الأربعة... وصححه ابن
-- خزيمة"). The import kept the matn verbatim and left `grading` empty, so the
-- information existed but could not be displayed, filtered or searched on its
-- own. Generated by scripts/extract_hadith_grading.ts (8 unit tests).
--
-- `arabic_text` is deliberately NOT touched. The clause is copied, not moved:
-- the matn as printed includes its takhrij, and mutating scripture-adjacent
-- text to populate a convenience field is not a trade worth making. Every value
-- below was verified to be a literal substring of its own entry's matn, so
-- nothing here is authored.
--
-- Keyed on (collection slug, entry number), NOT on entry id: ids are
-- `gen_random_uuid()` and differ per environment, so a UUID-keyed version
-- applied cleanly and updated zero rows on any database other than the one it
-- was generated from.
--
-- Coverage: 1358 of 1978 entries.
--   * The 620 without a grading are overwhelmingly العمدة (414 of them), which
--     carries no per-hadith takhrij at all — the work is *defined* as hadith
--     agreed upon by البخاري and مسلم, so it never repeats the attribution.
--     Stamping "متفق عليه" on those would be an editorial judgement, not an
--     extraction, and is left to the owner.
--   * The rest are بلوغ المرام continuation entries ("وفي رواية...", "وله
--     شاهد...") that hang off the preceding hadith and carry no ruling of their
--     own.
--
-- Idempotent: re-running rewrites the same values.

update content.hadith_entries e
set grading = v.grading
from (values
